1
00:00:00,175 --> 00:00:01,605
One falling
apple sparked

2
00:00:01,605 --> 00:00:02,885
the wildest question—

3
00:00:02,885 --> 00:00:04,123
does the Moon
fall too?

4
00:00:04,575 --> 00:00:05,505
Impossible, Newton!

5
00:00:05,505 --> 00:00:06,403
What holds
the Moon up?

6
00:00:06,975 --> 00:00:07,695
Invisible gravity—

7
00:00:07,695 --> 00:00:08,986
every mass pulls
every other mass!

8
00:00:09,625 --> 00:00:11,085
Next, Newton
shot sunlight

9
00:00:11,085 --> 00:00:12,305
through a glass prism—

10
00:00:12,305 --> 00:00:13,505
splitting white light

11
00:00:13,505 --> 00:00:14,983
into seven
rainbow colors!

12
00:00:15,625 --> 00:00:16,975
Every action
triggers an equal,

13
00:00:16,975 --> 00:00:17,796
opposite reaction—

14
00:00:18,175 --> 00:00:19,095
Whoa! That steel ball

15
00:00:19,095 --> 00:00:20,196
nearly knocked me over!

16
00:00:20,625 --> 00:00:22,445
Gravity bends
a fall into orbit—

17
00:00:22,445 --> 00:00:23,655
uniting falling apples

18
00:00:23,655 --> 00:00:24,996
and moons
under one law!

19
00:00:25,625 --> 00:00:27,435
Rockets, satellites,
Moon landings today—

20
00:00:27,435 --> 00:00:29,184
every launch flies
on Isaac Newton's laws.
